      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It has been removed on build 968 (6th August 2020), note from changelog for it:\nChanges\n- The Remeasure Avatar State Behavior has been removed pending redesign and re-implementation\n  - The initial implementation was experimental, insufficient in filling its purpose, and had more than a fair share of design and integration issues\n  - We plan on redesigning this feature and re-implementing it in a more functional, less buggy manner that will support a wider range of use cases, and be tolerant to continued updates and upgrades.\nhttps://discord.com/channels/189511567539306508/503009489486872583/741052636354183169",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-04-06T19:45:55.503Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In the early builds of Avatars 3.0, we had this handy animation state behavior allowed for whole avatars to be resized right from your expressions menu—and your viewpoint would scale with it creating a true and seamless avatar resizing experience.\n\nRemeasure Avatar was a state behavior and it recalibrated the position of an avatar's viewpoint. Simply, my request is that it be reintroduced into the VRCSDK.\n\nWhat I don't understand is why it had to go. This seamless avatar scaling was seriously the talk of the town before release candidate. The majority of discussions in the dedicated Discord channel for Avatars 3.0 was about the avatar scaler tools. Even today, I can find countless avatars in worlds that have scale parameters left over from that bygone era. If it was so popular, then why was it excluded from the release candidate? Is this just another chairs on avatars situation? I personally feel strongly about this feature and I feel like reintroducing it will make many-a avatar makers' days.\nThanks for reading my ted talk fellas! :)",
